 ## Version log
 
+### 2026-08-27, The 2026-08-25 batch is validated, and six reporting defects the review of it found (branch `OSP-boat-count-incorporation`)
+
+`06_diagnostics/run_patch_validation_2026-08-25.R` completed all six model-runs (~15 h). The batch is behaviour-neutral where it claims to be, every change moved for its predicted reason, and the two independent tracks reconcile to 0.73%. **Rung 4 is the shipped configuration and the new authoritative run: port total 66,237 (95% CI 50,037 - 91,210), effort 40,187, 4 of 4 components fitted.** Full numbers in `development_notes/PIPELINE_STATUS.md`; the review is `development_notes/ladder-validation-review-2026-08-27.md`; the sequenced follow-up work is `development_notes/improvement-plan-2026-08-27.md`.
+
+-   **The shipped config moves the port total DOWN 1.6% (pooled) and 1.1% (gear).** Decomposition: boat all-gear -1,882 at the weekend rung, boat pot closure +744 at the interview-floor rung, shore roughly +190 net, commercial census -165. The weekend redefinition, acting through the boat, is the whole story.
+-   **Baseline reproduction passes on both tracks, and the gear track is BIT-identical at the fit level.** All 1,508 / 4,935 / 3,431 parameter rows shared with the reference match at full double precision across the three fits; `convergence_report.csv` is byte-identical. The only differences are three new inert reporters (`f_lower[1]`, `f_lower_out[1]`, `osp_f_kappa_out`, all exactly 0 with 0 SD) and one pure rename, `f_crab_param[1]` -> `f_theta[1]`, identical to every digit. Pooled sits 11 crab (0.1 MCSE) from its reference, exactly as the retired `B3` dimension predicts.
+-   **The shore I/E unit fix is confirmed and large.** `sigma_IE` falls 1.068 -> 0.300 pooled and 0.871 -> 0.598 gear. It also checks out arithmetically: the geometric-mean ratio of crabber-hours to crabber-trips across the four in-window I/E days is 3.44, and `log(3.44) = 1.24` against a pre-fix `sigma_IE` of 1.03 to 1.07 -- a single lognormal scale absorbing a systematic unit offset of exactly that size. **Correction: the mismatch measures ~3.2x, not the ~4x estimated on 2026-08-25.**
+-   **One fit was lost, to one stalled chain.** Rung 2's shore all-gear was rejected by the gate (2,957 divergences, `E_sum` n_eff 30, R-hat 1.049), and that PE substitution is the entire rung-2 port drop. Per-chain, chains 1/2/4 recorded 163/140/154 divergences in line with rung 1's 385 across four, while chain 3 recorded 2,500 of 2,500 with mean accept-stat 0.053. It never moved. Re-running rung 2 on a different `bss_seed` is plan item 1.2.
+-   **Weekend = Sat/Sun does what was predicted, slightly past the forecast.** `B1` 1.67x -> 2.48x on shore all-gear against a predicted ~2.34x; boat all-gear 1.56x -> 1.90x. Boat all-gear catch falls 6.8%, which was not predicted and is the largest single move in the ladder.
+-   **The interview floor is a clean win.** The boat pot closure reaches the sampler and PASSES the gate (35 divergences, 0.58%, R-hat 1.0003, n_eff 5,207), reporting 850 (95% CI 274 - 2,693) against a PE of 400. Rungs 3 and 4 are numerically identical on the three fits they share, so the floor did exactly one thing. Roughly 18% of the port total previously carried no uncertainty at all.
+-   **RETRACTION.** The 2026-08-25 claim that the fixed shore I/E stream "becomes genuinely informative about `tau_shore`" is wrong as the model is written. `crab_bss_pooled.stan:370,418` declares `vector[D * estimate_L] L_raw` with `L[d] = L_data[d] * exp(L_prior_sigma[d] * L_raw[d])`; there is no shared `tau_shore` parameter, so four I/E days can inform four days out of 289. The season median `L` is 1.6998 against a prior centre of 1.7000. Making that claim true is a model change, not a config change (plan item 2.1).
+-   **Two criteria were wrong and are repaired.** The gear exactness criterion demanded `delta == 0` on the port total and FAILED at -19 while the model was bit-identical; the port total is assembled from `rstan::extract(permuted = TRUE)` draws and an unseeded `sample.int()`, which this document had already recorded as RNG-sensitive. Exactness is now tested on `convergence_report.csv` byte equality plus full-precision equality of every shared parameter row. The tau criterion is retired to INFO. A per-rung convergence criterion is added, because nothing in the original set noticed that rung 2 had lost a fit.
+-   **Six reporting defects fixed.** The second copy of the shore day-length weighting in `.srd_monthly_share()` (defect (B) was fixed in `pe_monthly_effort_share.R` only); the empty-effort-stratum report, which never reached a pooled run because that PE chunk is `results='hide'` and is now a CSV from both drivers; I/E unit provenance in `fit_data_summary.csv` plus `ie_trips` / `turnover` / `hours_per_trip` in the two I/E files; a `decoupled` flag on `structural_params_*.csv`; `production_arm` split per estimator; and an explicit `status = "skipped"` row when a CPUE regression falls below its 30-interview minimum.
+-   **The empty-stratum fix produced a finding immediately.** On the shipped config the zeroed-day shares are shore all-gear 44/289 (15.2%), boat pot closure 9/76 (11.8%), boat all-gear 47/289 (16.3%). Three of four components are above the 5% warning threshold at the default `zero` fill, and the figure previously on the record was the boat pot closure alone.
+-   **The largest open item is pre-existing and not in this batch: `osp_scale_is_tau` does not do what the notes say.** With it on, the OSP mean uses `L`, which is the same per-day independent construction as the retraction above, so 148 days of OSP data leave the posterior median at 1.201 against a prior centre of 1.200. The overlap calibration and the Phase-1 free `kappa_OSP` both put the real turnover at 2.0 to 3.0, and that conflict is absorbed by `r_OSP` (1.58 to 1.62) rather than moving `L`. Corroborating: the boat trailer PIT mean is 0.420 to 0.425 in all six runs against a nominal 0.50. The toggle roughly doubles the private-boat harvest, and as implemented the size of the doubling is set by the `tau_boat` prior rather than by OSP.
+-   Files changed: `03_R_functions/save_run_diagnostics.R`, `model_diagnostics.R`, `bss_day_length.R`, `bss_cpue_diagnostics.R`, `diagnose_incomplete_trips.R`, `run_pe_pooled.R`, `run_pe_gear.R`, `prep_bss_crab_pooled.R`, `prep_bss_crab_gear.R`; both drivers; `06_diagnostics/run_patch_validation_2026-08-25.R`, `test_improvements_2026-08-25.R`; new `development_notes/improvement-plan-2026-08-27.md` and `ladder-validation-review-2026-08-27.md`; `PIPELINE_STATUS.md`; `README-R-functions.md`; this history.
+
 ### 2026-08-26, Blocking defect in the 2026-08-25 batch: five Stan data variables declared but never passed (branch `OSP-boat-count-incorporation`)
 
 The 2026-08-25 batch was run through its own validation ladder (`06_diagnostics/run_patch_validation_2026-08-25.R`) and **every one of the six model-runs failed on its first BSS fit**, on both tracks and in every configuration, with `dim(X) must have a positive length`. No fitted results were produced; the partial folders under `05_output/20260825/` are scratch.
